# Employee Burnout Survey (Outdated Version)

**Date Sent:** 2026-03-28  
**Author:** Hiroshi Takahashi, HR Department

---

## Introduction
This survey was designed to assess employee burnout levels and gather feedback on workplace conditions and stressors. However, it has come to our attention that this version of the survey is outdated and does not reflect recent organizational updates or initiatives. We sincerely apologize for any confusion caused.

While this document is no longer valid, we are providing its content for transparency and record-keeping purposes. Please disregard this survey if you received it and refer to the corrected version, which will be sent shortly.

---

## Survey Objectives
The primary objectives of this survey are:

- To measure current burnout levels among employees.
- To identify key stressors affecting workplace morale and productivity.
- To collect actionable feedback on mitigating burnout and improving employee well-being.

---

## Instructions
*Please complete the following survey questions based on your experiences over the past three months. Your responses will remain anonymous and will be used solely to guide HR initiatives.*

---

## Survey Questions

### Section 1: General Well-Being
1. On a scale of 1 to 10, how would you rate your overall well-being at work?
   - [ ] 1 (Very Poor)
   - [ ] 2
   - [ ] 3
   - [ ] 4
   - [ ] 5
   - [ ] 6
   - [ ] 7
   - [ ] 8
   - [ ] 9
   - [ ] 10 (Excellent)

2. How frequently do you feel overwhelmed by your workload?
   - [ ] Never
   - [ ] Rarely
   - [ ] Sometimes
   - [ ] Often
   - [ ] Always

3. How would you describe your overall work-life balance?
   - [ ] Very Poor
   - [ ] Poor
   - [ ] Average
   - [ ] Good
   - [ ] Excellent

### Section 2: Workplace Stressors
4. Which of the following factors contribute most to your levels of stress at work? (Select all that apply)
   - [ ] High workload
   - [ ] Tight deadlines
   - [ ] Lack of resources
   - [ ] Poor communication within teams
   - [ ] Lack of recognition
   - [ ] Unclear expectations
   - [ ] Other: ______________________

5. How often do you feel supported by your manager or supervisor?
   - [ ] Never
   - [ ] Rarely
   - [ ] Sometimes
   - [ ] Often
   - [ ] Always

6. Do you feel that your concerns about workplace stress are taken seriously by leadership?
   - [ ] Yes
   - [ ] No
   - [ ] Unsure

### Section 3: Burnout Indicators
7. Have you experienced any of the following symptoms of burnout in the past three months? (Select all that apply)
   - [ ] Emotional exhaustion
   - [ ] Lack of motivation
   - [ ] Reduced productivity
   - [ ] Physical symptoms (e.g., headaches, fatigue)
   - [ ] Cynicism or detachment
   - [ ] None of the above

8. On average, how many hours do you work per week?
   - [ ] Less than 30 hours
   - [ ] 30-40 hours
   - [ ] 41-50 hours
   - [ ] 51-60 hours
   - [ ] More than 60 hours

9. Have you considered leaving your current role due to burnout?
   - [ ] Yes
   - [ ] No
   - [ ] Unsure

### Section 4: Feedback and Suggestions
10. What changes would you recommend to reduce burnout and improve workplace well-being? (Open-ended)
   - ______________________________________________________
   - ______________________________________________________
   - ______________________________________________________

